  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Line is passing through intersection of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,</p><p>So its equation is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And the line is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now putting the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;in equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is tangent to circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>17</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now eccentricity of the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>",
